Below is a practical, step‑by‑step guide you can follow to build a modern, production‑ready frontend for your e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole pipeline—from planning and design to coding, testing, and deployment—so you can pick the parts that fit your team’s skill set and project scope.

---

## 1️⃣ Planning & Requirements

| What | Why | How |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Define core features** | Shopping cart, product catalog, search, filters, checkout, user accounts, reviews, admin panel, analytics | List them in a product backlog; prioritize by business value |
| **Identify target devices** | Desktop, tablet, mobile | Decide if you’ll build a PWA or native‑like SPA |
| **Set performance goals** | First Contentful Paint < 2 s, Time to Interactive < 5 s | Use Lighthouse benchmarks |
| **Accessibility & SEO** | WCAG 2.1 AA, semantic HTML, server‑side rendering | Plan for ARIA roles, meta tags, structured data |

> **Tip:** Create a *feature map* (e.g., a Trello board) so everyone sees what’s coming next.

---

## 2️⃣ Wireframes & Prototypes

| Tool | Use‑case | Why |
|------|----------|-----|
| **Figma / Sketch / Adobe XD** | Low‑fidelity wireframes → High‑fidelity prototypes | Collaboration, component libraries |
| **Storybook** | Isolated UI components | Visual regression, documentation |
| **InVision / Marvel** | Interactive prototypes for stakeholder demos | Clickable flows, user testing |

**Workflow:**

1. Sketch the main pages: Home, Category, Product Detail, Cart, Checkout, Profile, Admin Dashboard.
2. Add interactive elements: search bar, filter panel, pagination, modal dialogs.
3. Export assets (icons, images) or use an icon library (Heroicons, Font Awesome).

---

## 3️⃣ Choose Your Tech Stack

| Layer | Options | Recommendation |
|-------|---------|----------------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular | **React** (most popular, huge ecosystem) |
| **State Management** | Redux Toolkit, Zustand, Recoil, Vuex | **Redux Toolkit** (simple, built‑in devtools) |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules, Styled‑Components, Tailwind CSS, SCSS | **Tailwind CSS** (utility‑first, fast prototyping) |
| **Routing** | React Router, Vue Router, Angular Router | **React Router v6** |
| **API Client** | Axios, Fetch, SWR, React Query | **React Query** (caching, background refetch) |
| **Form Handling** | Formik, React Hook Form | **React Hook Form** (lightweight, good validation) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library, Cypress | Unit + E2E: Jest + RTL + Cypress |
| **Build Tool** | Vite, Next.js, CRA | **Next.js** (SSR, SSG, API routes, image optimization) |
| **Deployment** | Vercel, Netlify, Cloudflare Pages | **Vercel** (native Next.js support) |

> **Why Next.js?**  
> • Server‑Side Rendering (SEO friendly)  
> • Static Site Generation for product pages (fast)  
> • Built‑in Image Optimization  
> • API Routes for simple backend logic (e.g., webhook handlers)

---

## 4️⃣ Project Skeleton (Next.js + React)

```bash
npx create-next-app@latest ecommerce-frontend --typescript
cd ecommerce-frontend
npm install tailwindcss postcss autoprefixer
npx tailwindcss init -p
```

