## 🔟 Accessibility & SEO

| Checklist | Implementation |
|-----------|----------------|
| **Semantic HTML** | Use `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<footer>` |
| **Alt Text** | `next/image` automatically generates alt attributes |
| **Keyboard Navigation** | Ensure focus states, use `tabIndex` where needed |
| **ARIA Roles** | `role="button"`, `aria-label`, `aria-live` for dynamic updates |
| **Meta Tags** | `next/head` for title, description, Open Graph |
| **Structured Data** | JSON‑LD for products (`product.jsonld`) |
| **Image Optimization** | `next/image` with `layout="responsive"` |

---

## 🧪 Testing Strategy

| Test Type | Tool | Example |
|-----------|------|---------|
| Unit | Jest + React Testing Library | Test component rendering, props |
| Integration | React Testing Library + MSW (Mock Service Worker) | Mock API responses |
| End‑to‑End | Cypress | Simulate user flow: add to cart → checkout |
| Visual Regression | Chromatic (Storybook) | Detect UI drift |

**Sample unit test**

```tsx
// __tests__/ProductCard.test.tsx
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import ProductCard from '../components/ProductCard';

test('renders product title and price', () => {
  const product = { id: '1', title: 'Test Shirt', price: 29.99 };
  render(<ProductCard product={product} />);
  expect(screen.getByText(/Test Shirt/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
  expect(screen.getByText(/\$29\.99/i)).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

